- Business Rules: N/A
- Assumptions: The system is functioning correctly, and session handling is active.
- Open Issues: None

## LeftNav-UC4 — Switch User

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): System
- Trigger: User selects the switch user option.
- Description: Allows a user to switch to a different user profile or ID.
- Preconditions: User is logged into the system and has permission to switch users.
- Postconditions: User is logged as a new user ID.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User clicks on the switch user button.
  2. System processes the switch using `goBackToPrimaryID`.
  3. User is logged in with the new ID.
- Extensions: N/A
- Exceptions:
  - If switching fails, an appropriate error message is displayed.
- Business Rules: User must have permissions to switch.
- Assumptions: The system maintains multiple user profiles.
- Open Issues: None

## LeftNav-UC5 — Set Start Page

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: User selects the make start page option.
- Description: Sets the current page as the start page for the user's session.
- Preconditions: User is logged into the system.
- Postconditions: The selected page is set as the start page for future sessions.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User clicks the make start page button.
  2. System sets the current page as the start page using `SetStartScreen`.
- Extensions: N/A
- Exceptions:
  - If the start page setting fails, an error is returned to the user.
- Business Rules: N/A
- Assumptions: User has the permission to set their start page.
- Open Issues: None

